  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 258 AM EDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will begin to build on Wednesday as the much-\ndiscussed Nor'easter drifts north and dissipates. Near the surface, \nhigh pressure will continue to build across the western Atlantic, \nbringing the return of easterly/southeasterly flow across the area. \nMoisture advection will continue, with PWATs forecast to continue \nhovering near 2 inches through the period. This pattern will promote \ncontinued scattered to widespread shower and thunderstorm \ndevelopment each afternoon. Storm activity will likely favor \ninterior and southwestern Florida due to the stronger easterly flow \nduring the latter half of the week. There is increasing confidence \nthat temperatures will increase back into the upper 80s and low 90s \nareawide over the weekend.",
